WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.351
Tool-assisted detection helps teams find
heap memory defects earlier.

2
00:00:04.431 --> 00:00:09.039
AddressSanitizer-style diagnostics can
expose invalid heap access during executed

3
00:00:09.119 --> 00:00:09.498
tests.

4
00:00:09.578 --> 00:00:13.176
Leak detection can highlight missing
cleanup, unclear ownership,

5
00:00:13.256 --> 00:00:16.159
or failure paths that do not release
allocated memory.

6
00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:20.469
Static analysis can flag risky patterns
such as unchecked allocation results,

7
00:00:20.549 --> 00:00:24.526
suspicious size calculations, possible
stale use, double cleanup paths,

8
00:00:24.606 --> 00:00:25.805
and missing releases.

9
00:00:25.885 --> 00:00:29.736
Compiler warnings can also reveal
conversions, ignored return values,

10
00:00:29.816 --> 00:00:31.836
and assumptions that deserve review.

11
00:00:31.916 --> 00:00:36.334
Debug allocators and targeted runtime
checks can support focused investigation.

12
00:00:36.414 --> 00:00:39.949
They can help reveal misuse in development
and test environments,

13
00:00:40.029 --> 00:00:44.196
especially when paired with meaningful
test inputs and repeatable commands.

14
00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:48.126
The exact tools depend on compiler,
platform, and project constraints.

15
00:00:48.206 --> 00:00:51.552
Tools are powerful, but they do not prove
every heap use is safe.

16
00:00:51.632 --> 00:00:54.283
They detect what they can observe or
reason about.

17
00:00:54.363 --> 00:00:58.908
Untested paths, unsupported build
configurations, uninstrumented dependencies,

18
00:00:58.988 --> 00:01:01.450
and unclear contracts can still hide
defects.

19
00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:05.002
A mature workflow combines tools with
design, tests, and review.

20
00:01:05.082 --> 00:01:08.364
Findings should lead to root-cause fixes,
regression tests,

21
00:01:08.444 --> 00:01:10.401
and clearer ownership conventions.

22
00:01:10.481 --> 00:01:12.564
The goal is not only to close one report,

23
00:01:12.644 --> 00:01:14.980
but to make the next mistake easier to
catch.
